  "evidence": "P2 shows a large, sustained E/U offset (≈27 mm E, −13 mm U) from index ~467 to ~526, with interior points consistently elevated in E and depressed in U relative to surrounding motion; P1’s smaller offset (−0.6/2.0/0.6 mm) is inconsistent with the dominant signal and likely contaminated by the same event or local noise. The onset estimate for P2 aligns with a sharp step at index 467 in E/U, and return is evident near 526–527 where E drops back toward pre-event levels and U recovers. A nuisance step at day 490 (per numerical tool) does not invalidate the platform—it may be an independent small step within the temporary offset interval. P1 overlaps and is weaker; no evidence supports it as a separate genuine platform. Thus only P2 is retained as a genuine temporary platform.",
  "pair_ids": ["P2"]
}
